# uhd_rfsoc.conf -- board-local settings of the UHD daemon (ZCU216 or RFSoC 4x2).
#
# Copy to uhd_rfsoc.conf (next to uhd_rfsoc_daemon.py, or /etc/uhd_rfsoc.conf,
# or point $UHD_RFSOC_CONF at it; rfsoc/setup_board.sh makes the copy) and
# fill in. uhd_rfsoc.conf is git-ignored: addresses belong to the
# installation, not to the code.
#
# The board's LAN (management) address is NOT set here: the daemon answers
# discovery and control with whatever address the request arrived on, so a
# DHCP change needs nothing. Only the FPGA's 100G data-plane identity is
# configured, because the FPGA has no DHCP:
#
#   data_ip   the FPGA's IPv4 address on the 100G link. It must be on the
#             subnet of the PC's 100G port, which host/setup_cx5.sh <iface>
#             <host-data-ip>/<prefix> configures. REQUIRED in hardware mode.
#   data_mac  the FPGA's MAC on the 100G link. Optional: by default a locally
#             administered MAC derived from the board's eth0 MAC.
#   name      discovery name (UHD device arg name=). Optional, default the
#             board's: zcu216 or rfsoc4x2.
#   clock_source  the reference of the board's LMK04828, applied at every
#             bring-up. external (default): the reference input (the 10 MHz
#             of a GPSDO shared by several boards: CLK104 REF IN on a ZCU216,
#             the reference SMA on an RFSoC 4x2); the LMK04828 falls back to
#             the board's own oscillator by itself when there is no
#             reference. internal: the board's oscillator only.
#
# Command-line --data-ip / --data-mac / --name / --clock-source override these.

data_ip  = <fpga-data-ip>
# data_mac = <fpga-data-mac>
# name     = <device-name>
# clock_source = internal
